#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hil - shared hardware-in-the-loop bench control.

Drives a board's power switch and debug UART so any project (or agent) can
power-cycle a target, capture its boot console, and assert it reached a
login prompt. Machine-specific values live in ~/.config/hil-bench/benches.toml,
never in this tool.

    hil [-b BENCH] power status|on|off|cycle
    hil power watch [--interval S] [--duration S] [--csv FILE]
    hil boot   [--no-cycle] [--repeat N] [--power-interval S] [--timeout S] [--log-dir DIR] [--json]
    hil uboot  env|slot A|B|reset-counters|run -c CMD...|shell  [--then boot|stay|reset]
    hil wait-ssh [--host H] [--timeout S]
    hil console [--log-dir DIR]
    hil benches

Exit status: 0 pass, 1 target failed a check, 2 bench/config/infra error,
3 bench is locked by another run.
"""

